#* {{RQ:Telegraph|date=May 9, 2012|author=John Percy| title=Birmingham City 2 Blackpool 2 (2-3 on agg): match report| url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/competitions/championship/9254026/Birmingham-City-2-Blackpool-2-2-3-on-agg-match-report.html| passage=Blackpool continue to thrive on the adrenalin rush of the end-of-season shoot-out and are heading for a second Wembley date in two years after negotiating a '''nervy''' path past Birmingham.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251116135702/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/competitions/championship/9254026/Birmingham-City-2-Blackpool-2-2-3-on-agg-match-report.html|archivedate=16 November 2025}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|date=2022-08-24|author=w:Peter Bradshaw|title=Mr Malcolm’s List review – Regency romcom served with cake-icing of irony|url=https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/aug/24/mr-malcolms-list-review-regency-romcom-served-with-cake-icing-of-irony|passage=She has been asked on a date to see {{w|The Barber of Seville}} in the company of society’s wealthiest and most eligible bachelor, the Hon Jeremy Malcolm ({{w|Ṣọpẹ́ Dìrísù}}) who is bored by her '''nervy''' and untutored chatter.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261017051709/https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/aug/24/mr-malcolms-list-review-regency-romcom-served-with-cake-icing-of-irony|archivedate=17 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[strong|Strong]]; [[sinewy]].
